OL,3,AOur Friends in the North still relevant
OL,4,A- writer
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe writer of acclaimed 1990s BBC TV
OL,7,Fdrama Our Friends in the North has said
OL,8,Fa new stage version will resonate with
OL,9,Fmodern audiences, even if he had once
OL,10,Fthought its themes would become
OL,11,Firrelevant.
OL,13,FPeter Flannery, who was born and raised
OL,14,Fin Jarrow, said he had hoped the
OL,15,Fcorruption and poverty the original
OL,16,Fshow explored in the North East would
OL,17,Ffade away.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,170,160,200,105,0,100
